The example in examples/guardrail_agent, which is in the source repository
and not in the PyPI package, includes four files taken from frontier-scout
(https://github.com/ajaysurya1221/frontier-scout) at commit 58b0b17 (the
same content is on its main branch at commit 042bdfd),
Copyright (c) 2026 Frontier Scout contributors, MIT License: hook_runtime.py
(frontier_scout/agent_firewall/hook_runtime.py, unchanged below a five-line
header that says so), policy.json (frontier-scout.policy.json, unchanged),
commands.jsonl (docs/evaluation/decision-model/commands.jsonl, unchanged)
and answers.jsonl (docs/evaluation/decision-model/answers.jsonl, unchanged).
The example's README gives the SHA-256 of each file as it is in
frontier-scout; for hook_runtime.py that is the hash without the header.

The results under docs/results/jev-calibration, which are in the source
repository and not in the PyPI package, use the intent label names of the
CLINC150 dataset (Larson et al., 2019) and the Banking77 dataset (Casanueva
et al., 2020), both CC BY licensed and credited in
bench/jev_calibration/PROTOCOL.md. The dataset texts are not included.

